Package: popreconlite
Title: Population Reconstruction by Cohort Components Between Censuses
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Percy", "Soto-Becerra", email = "percys1991@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Reconstructs populations between censuses by cohort components at single
    years of age and annual steps, for both sexes and for areas linked by
    internal migration, with net migration estimated and with paired draws,
    following the approach described for the Global Burden of Disease (GBD)
    study. Development version: the shared infrastructure (draws container,
    per-cell seeds, age groups, simulated country with planted truth) is
    implemented; the estimation functions are documented skeletons. This
    package is an independent implementation. It is not affiliated with,
    endorsed by, or supported by the Institute for Health Metrics and
    Evaluation (IHME), and it does not contain IHME code or data. It is not
    a successor of the 'popReconstruct' package.
